From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: AC-PHY: mdelay instead of a 5.85 ms udelay (ARM)

ARM rejects udelay() constants above 2000 us at link time
(__bad_udelay); mdelay(6) busy-waits the same way and covers the 5848 us of
the capture. The same change is in b43-ac-wip as #15.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
index 190afa0..0fba895 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
@@ -2878,7 +2878,8 @@ static void b43_phy_ac_rxcore_setstate(struct b43_wldev *dev, u8 coremask)
 	 * read after. The capture delays 5848 us after the wide-open write.
 	 */
 	b43_phy_write(dev, 0x16d8, 0xffff);
-	udelay(5850);
+	/* ARM has no udelay() above 2 ms (__bad_udelay) */
+	mdelay(6);
 
 	b43_phy_maskset(dev, 0x0160, (u16)~0x0007, coremask);
 	b43_phy_maskset(dev, B43_PHY_AC_RF_SEQ_MODE, (u16)~0x0070,
